  _isSmallIngredient: 0
  _recipeBookDescriptionUnspoiled: The pairing of the salty cheese and the filling
    bread has a history as ancient as the sun and the moon. Some people lauded it
    as the perfect dish to encapsulate old Verehn, the rich cheese complementing
    the baked, tasteless bread and the latter stretching the supply of the other.
    These people were probably the nobles, who had the spare time to muse about their
    meal instead of struggling to find their next one.
  _recipeBookDescriptionSpoiled: Haughty nobles used to put stinky cheese on sour
    bread, which was alien to everyone but them. This might either be an attempt
    to emulate that, or just a happy coincidence. Nevertheless, the sharp and tangy
    cheese could only be dampened by the texture of stale bread, which somehow makes
    the dish the more popular option for people who salivate for the more decadent
    or decayed things in life. Whoever they are, the government will be watching
    them.
